    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6459A\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the town of Clarkstown to offer a certain retirement\noption to Clarkstown police officers Edward Fairclough, Kyle McKiernan,\nCorry Doyle, and Sean Weaver\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThe town of Clarkstown is authorized to offer a certain retirement\noption to Clarkstown police officers Edward Fairclough, Kyle NcKiernan,\nCorry Doyle, and Sean Weaver\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one authorizes the town of Clarkstown to offer a certain retire-\nment option to Clarkstown police officers Edward Fairclough, Kyle\nMchiernan, Corry Doyle, and Sean Weaver\n\nSection two: All past service costs associated with implementing the\nprovisions of this act shall be borne by the town of Clarkstown.\n\nSection three of the bill relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFor reasons not ascribable to their own negligence, police officers\nEdward Fairclough, Kyle McKiernan, Corry Doyle and Sean Weaver failed to\nmake a timely application to participate in the 384-d optional retire-\nment plan. The officers shall be entitled to the full rights and bene-\nfits associated with coverage by filing a request to that effect with\nthe state comptroller within one year of the effective date of this act.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE:\n\nFiscal Note t-'2020-46 Prepared by OSC February 24, 2020.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
